# Konsolai

## GIT CONVENTION (applies to every commit, now and in future tasks)
- Branch: dev. One commit per file changed.
- All commits go to dev. Never commit to prod; prod only receives merges done by the user.
- Message format:
 [TYPE|SIZE] Title in imperative mood, max 72 chars
 <blank line>
 Body: what changed and why, as short lines or "- " bullets.
- TYPE is one of: ADD, UPDATE, FIX, DELETE, MOVE, REFACTOR
- SIZE: MINOR (<20 changed lines), MEDIUM (20-100), MAJOR (>100, or a public API or behavior change)
- Use: git commit -F <msgfile> (do not cram the body into -m)
- Never commit secrets, binaries or files outside the repo (~/.bashrc and similar are not part of the repo).

## Stack
- Go 1.27, stdlib only unless the architect approves a dependency.
- Approved: github.com/jackc/pgx/v5 (pgxpool). Raw SQL only; no ORM; no migration library.
- Approved: github.com/alecthomas/chroma/v2 (code-block highlighting only).
- Approved: github.com/yuin/goldmark (with its built-in GFM extension).
- Approved: github.com/reeflective/readline (REPL line editor only).
- Module github.com/siraj/konsolai.

## Layout
- cmd/konsolai (entrypoint)
- internal/config (XDG config.json profiles)
- internal/redact (secrets before persist)
- internal/store (Postgres via pgxpool; best-effort, 2s timeouts)
- internal/memory (adapters; agent/tools/ui never import pgx)
- internal/llm (model client)
- internal/sysctx (environment context)
- internal/safety (command and path guard)
- internal/diff (Myers unified diffs)
- internal/repo (root, file listing, project detect)
- internal/intent (router)
- internal/docrender (markdown/mermaid/HTML/PDF for export_doc)
- internal/tools (run_shell, write_file, read_file, list_dir, search, find_files, edit_file, propose_plan, remember, web_fetch, export_doc, outline, finish)
- internal/agent (tool-calling loop)
- internal/ui (TTY prompt and ANSI)
- internal/turn (one request: Runner.RunTurn)
- internal/commands (slash-command registry; REPL reuses it)
- internal/clip (clipboard: wl-copy, xclip, xsel, OSC 52)
- internal/repl (interactive TTY loop; LineReader + reeflective/readline)
- New packages only when the architect specifies them.
- Grammar:
 konsolai [--yes] [--profile NAME] [--intent answer|lookup|act|build] [--trace] [--plain] [--version] [new] ["<request>"]
 konsolai [--profile NAME] /<command> [args]
 konsolai [--profile NAME] history | undo | facts | prune
 konsolai [--profile NAME] remember [--project] "<fact>"
 konsolai [--profile NAME] forget user|project <id>
 No request and stdin+stdout are TTYs: REPL. No request and a pipe: stdin is the request.
 A request and a pipe: stdin is attached as context.
- answer: stream, no tools. lookup: read-only tools, ExploreBudget 6, MaxSteps 10.
 act: all tools, no plan, ExploreBudget 6, MaxSteps 15.
 build: plan gate, ExploreBudget 12, MaxSteps 60, thinking, temp 0.3.
- Memory: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/konsolai/config.json (default ~/.config/konsolai/config.json).
 --profile beats KONSOLAI_PROFILE beats default_profile beats built-in "default".
 KONSOLAI_DATABASE_URL / KONSOLAI_ENDPOINT / KONSOLAI_MODEL override profile fields.
 Resume the latest active|finished session (one family; mode ignored)
 within session_idle_minutes unless `new` or the session is closed (`/new`).
 Title is set only at CreateSession.
 Store the intent in sessions.mode. Redact only what is persisted. On first
 store failure, one dim line
 "memory disabled: cannot connect to <host:port>: <innermost cause>".
- Version: `var version = "dev"` in cmd/konsolai, stamped via
  `-ldflags "-X main.version=$(git describe --tags --always --dirty)"`.
  `scripts/build.sh` builds with `-trimpath -ldflags "-s -w -X main.version=..."`
  to `~/.local/bin/konsolai`. `konsolai --version` and `/status` show it.
- Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 error, 2 usage, 3 aborted, 4 max steps, 130 cancelled.

## Server
- vLLM at http://fatboy:11436/v1, model qwen38.nvfp4, max_model_len 94208.
- Thinking is controlled by chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking.
- Reasoning arrives in delta.reasoning.

## Code rules
- Strict types, no interface{}/any unless unavoidable.
- Wrap errors with a "pkg: context: %w" prefix.
- No debug logging, no unrequested features.
- Do not touch files outside the task scope.

## Workflow
- After every task run gofmt -l ., go vet ./..., go build -o ~/.local/bin/konsolai ./cmd/konsolai.
- If anything fails, stop and report it. Do not improvise fixes.

## Test database
- NEVER start, stop, restart or remove the user's container `konsolai-pg` (port 55432, volume konsolai-pg).
- Integration tests use a separate throwaway container. Bring it up and down with `scripts/test-db.sh up` / `down`.
 docker run -d --rm --name konsolai-pg-test --network host \
 -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=ktest -e POSTGRES_DB=konsolai_test -e PGPORT=55433 pgvector/pgvector:pg17
 KONSOLAI_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:ktest@localhost:55433/konsolai_test?sslmode=disable
- End-to-end runs that need memory use the user's DB as-is, and must not depend on its contents.
